THE NARRATOR

The narrator is a synthetic voice, not a clone of any person's voice, and the same
narrator speaks the DDWG introduction films. Its identity recording,
assets/audio/narration-reference.wav, was generated from a text description of a voice
with Qwen3-TTS VoiceDesign through mlx-audio and selected by the author. The English
reference and the Mandarin references that the casts name were spoken in that voice by
the Qwen3-TTS Base model, which also narrates both editions. The natural Mandarin reference,
assets/audio/narration-reference-natural.wav, was derived from the identity recording in the
two recorded steps that content/voice-reference.json lists, with only its edges trimmed.

The pronunciation contract records, as listening targets, English stress from CMUdict at
commit 74790861, Copyright (C) 1993-2015 Carnegie Mellon University, under its
BSD-style license, Chinese readings from the macOS dictionaries, and the spoken forms
that the previous ETHOS introduction film adopted for the same narrator.
